<body>

<header>
  <p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> &gt; <a href="/lesson50">Projects &amp; Career</a> &gt; Lesson 50 - Final Exam &amp; Certificate</p>
  <p><a id="homeLink" href="/">← Back to Home</a> | Projects &amp; Career - Lesson 50 / 50 - FINAL</p>
  <h1>Lesson 50: Final Exam &amp; Certificate - You Did It! 🎓</h1>
  <p>Pass With 80% - Get Your Web Developer Certificate | LearnHTMLCSSJS.com</p>
  <% if (!user) { %>
    <p style="background:#2563eb;display:inline-block;padding:8px 16px;border-radius:20px;margin-top:10px;font-weight:bold">👋 Guest - Login to take Final Exam & Get Certificate</p>
  <% } else if (typeof canTakeExam !== 'undefined' && !canTakeExam) { %>
    <p style="background:#dc2626;display:inline-block;padding:8px 16px;border-radius:20px;margin-top:10px;font-weight:bold">🔒 Exam Locked - <%= passedCount %> / 49 Lessons Passed</p>
  <% } else if (typeof canTakeExam !== 'undefined' && canTakeExam) { %>
    <p style="background:#16a34a;display:inline-block;padding:8px 16px;border-radius:20px;margin-top:10px;font-weight:bold">✅ Exam Unlocked - You Passed All 49 Lessons!</p>
  <% } %>
  <% if (typeof existingCertificate !== 'undefined' && existingCertificate) { %>
    <p style="background:#f59e0b;color:#0f172a;display:inline-block;padding:8px 16px;border-radius:20px;margin-top:10px;font-weight:bold">🎓 You Already Have a Certificate! ID: <%= existingCertificate.certificateId %> | Score: <%= existingCertificate.score %>/100</p>
  <% } %>
</header>

<div class="container">
  <div class="tabs">
    <button id="lessonTabBtn" class="tab-btn active" onclick="showLesson()">📖 Lesson</button>
    <% if (typeof canTakeExam !== 'undefined' && canTakeExam) { %>
      <button id="testTabBtn" class="tab-btn" onclick="showTest()">📝 Final Exam - 100 Marks</button>
    <% } else { %>
      <button class="tab-btn disabled" title="Complete Lesson 1-49 with 80%+ first">🔒 Final Exam - LOCKED (<%= typeof passedCount !== 'undefined' ? passedCount : 0 %>/49)</button>
    <% } %>
  </div>
  <div id="lockMsg" class="lock-msg">🔒 Exam is running! All tabs are locked until you submit the exam or time ends.</div>

  <div id="lessonContent">
    <h2>1. Your Journey - From Zero to Web Developer</h2>
    <p>Look how far you have come. 50 lessons ago, you did not know what HTML was. Today you can build a complete website, with cart, filter, WhatsApp order, and deploy it LIVE.</p>
    <div class="journey"><div><b>1-10</b>HTML<br>Structure</div><div><b>11-20</b>CSS<br>Design</div><div><b>21-40</b>JavaScript<br>Logic</div><div><b>41-50</b>Projects &amp; Career<br>Money &amp; Job</div></div>
    <table>
      <tr><th>What You Can Do Now</th><th>Proof</th></tr>
      <tr><td>Build any website from scratch</td><td>Lesson 41 + 45 - Full Website + Final Project</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Build shop with cart + WhatsApp order</td><td>Lesson 45 - Fresh Mart Shop</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Build portfolio + landing page</td><td>Lesson 42 + 43</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Deploy website LIVE for free</td><td>Lesson 47 - Netlify</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Rank website on Google</td><td>Lesson 46 - SEO</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Get clients + earn money</td><td>Lesson 48 - Freelancing</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Pass interviews + get a job</td><td>Lesson 49 - Interview Qs</td></tr>
    </table>
    <div class="note"><b>Certificate is NOT the goal. Skill is the goal.</b> Certificate opens the door. Your projects get you the job. Show your portfolio + certificate together - That is unbeatable.</div>

    <h2>2. Your Certificate - Preview</h2>
    <% if (typeof canTakeExam !== 'undefined' && !canTakeExam) { %>
      <div class="locked-box">
        <h2>🔒 Certificate Locked</h2>
        <% if (!user) { %>
          <p>You are browsing as a <b>Guest</b>.</p>
          <p>To get your certificate, please <b>Signup Free</b>, then pass <b>all 49 lessons (Lesson 1 to 49) with 80% or more</b>, then come back here.</p>
          <a href="/signup" class="btn" style="background:#16a34a">✨ Signup Free & Start Lesson 1 →</a>
          <a href="/login" class="btn btn-next">Login →</a>
        <% } else { %>
          <p>You have passed <b><%= passedCount %> / 49</b> lessons.</p>
          <p>To unlock your certificate, you must pass <b>all 49 lessons (Lesson 1 to 49) with 80% or more.</b></p>
          <% if (typeof failedLessons !== 'undefined' && failedLessons.length > 0) { %>
            <p>Remaining Lessons: <b><%= failedLessons.join(', ') %></b></p>
          <% } %>
          <p>Complete the remaining lessons first, then come back here.</p>
          <a href="/dashboard" class="btn" style="background:#dc2626">📊 Check My Dashboard →</a>
          <a href="/lesson<%= (typeof failedLessons !== 'undefined' && failedLessons.length > 0) ? failedLessons[0] : 1 %>" class="btn btn-next">Continue Learning →</a>
        <% } %>
      </div>
    <% } else { %>
      <p>Pass the Final Exam below with 80% or more, enter your name, and your certificate will be generated here. You can print it or save as PDF:</p>
      <div class="demo-card">
        <div class="cert" id="certPreview">
          <div class="cert-badge">🎓</div>
          <p style="letter-spacing:3px;color:#92400e;font-weight:bold;margin:0">LEARNHTMLCSSJS.COM</p>
          <h2>Certificate of Completion</h2>
          <p style="margin:0;color:#64748b">This certificate is proudly presented to</p>
          <div class="cert-name" id="certName"><%= (typeof user !== 'undefined' && user) ? user.username : 'Your Name Here' %></div>
          <p style="margin:0">For successfully completing the <b>Complete HTML, CSS &amp; JavaScript Course</b><br>50 Lessons - From Zero to Web Developer</p>
          <p style="margin:10px 0 0"><b>Final Exam Score: <span id="certScore"><%= (typeof existingCertificate !== 'undefined' && existingCertificate) ? existingCertificate.score + ' / 100' : '___ / 100' %></span></b> &nbsp; | &nbsp; Grade: <b id="certGrade"><%= (typeof existingCertificate !== 'undefined' && existingCertificate) ? (existingCertificate.score >= 95 ? 'A+ - Outstanding!' : existingCertificate.score >= 90 ? 'A - Excellent!' : existingCertificate.score >= 85 ? 'B+ - Very Good!' : 'B - Good!') : '___' %></b></p>
          <p style="font-size:13px;color:#64748b;margin:8px 0 0">Skills: HTML • CSS • JavaScript • Portfolio • Landing Page • SEO • Deploy • Freelancing</p>
          <div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;margin-top:16px;font-size:13px;color:#475569;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:6px"><span>Date: <b id="certDate"><%= (typeof existingCertificate !== 'undefined' && existingCertificate && existingCertificate.date) ? new Date(existingCertificate.date).toLocaleDateString('en-GB',{day:'numeric',month:'long',year:'numeric'}) : '___' %></b></span><span>Certificate ID: <b id="certId"><%= (typeof existingCertificate !== 'undefined' && existingCertificate) ? existingCertificate.certificateId : 'LHCSJS-____' %></b></span><span>LearnHTMLCSSJS.com ✓</span></div>
          <p class="verify-line" id="verifyLine" style="<%= (typeof existingCertificate !== 'undefined' && existingCertificate) ? '' : 'display:none' %>">Verify this certificate at: <a id="verifyLink" href="/verify/<%= (typeof existingCertificate !== 'undefined' && existingCertificate) ? existingCertificate.certificateId : '' %>" target="_blank">learnhtmlcssjs.com/verify/<span id="verifyIdText"><%= (typeof existingCertificate !== 'undefined' && existingCertificate) ? existingCertificate.certificateId : '' %></span></a></p>
        </div>
        <div class="no-print" style="max-width:520px;margin:0 auto">
          <label style="font-size:13px;font-weight:bold">Enter Your Full Name for Certificate (As you want it printed)</label>
          <input class="demo-input" id="studentName" placeholder="e.g. Muhammad Ali Ahmed" value="<%= (typeof user !== 'undefined' && user) ? user.username : '' %>" oninput="updateCertName()">
          <button class="btn" onclick="updateCertName()">Update Name on Certificate ✏️</button>
          <button class="btn btn-next" onclick="window.print()">🖨️ Print / Save as PDF</button>
          <p style="font-size:13px;color:#64748b">Tip: After passing exam, your score will auto-fill here. Then Print → Save as PDF.</p>
          <% if (typeof existingCertificate !== 'undefined' && existingCertificate) { %>
            <p style="font-size:13px"><a href="/verify/<%= existingCertificate.certificateId %>" target="_blank" style="color:#2563eb;font-weight:bold">🔍 Verify My Certificate →</a></p>
          <% } %>
        </div>
      </div>
    <% } %>

    <h2>3. Exam Rules - Read Before Starting</h2>
    <p>1. <b>Total Questions:</b> 20 - From all 50 lessons - HTML, CSS, JS, Projects, Career<br>2. <b>Total Marks:</b> 100 - Each question = 5 Marks<br>3. <b>Passing Marks:</b> 80 (80%) - You need 16 correct out of 20<br>4. <b>Time:</b> 10 Minutes - Auto-submit when time ends<br>5. <b>Attempts:</b> Unlimited - If you fail, read lessons again and try again<br>6. <b>Certificate:</b> After passing, enter your name above, your score fills automatically, then Print / Save as PDF</p>

    <h2>4. What to Do AFTER Certificate - Your Next 30 Days</h2>
    <p><b>Week 1:</b> Deploy portfolio + Final Project. Add links to WhatsApp bio, Facebook bio, LinkedIn.<br><b>Week 2:</b> Visit 10 local shops. Show portfolio. Get first client - Even for Rs. 5,000.<br><b>Week 3:</b> Apply to 20 jobs - Rozee.pk, LinkedIn, Indeed - Junior Frontend / Web Developer. Post your certificate on LinkedIn.<br><b>Week 4:</b> Learn NEXT skill - React.js OR WordPress - One of them doubles your income. React = Jobs in companies. WordPress = Fast client websites.</p>
    <div class="box"><b>Remember:</b> You are NOT finished. You are STARTING. Certificate = Door opens. Projects = You walk through. Keep building, keep learning, keep sharing. One year from today, you will not believe how far you have come.</div>
    <p><b>Final Step:</b> Go to Final Exam below. Pass it. Get your certificate. Then go get your first client.</p>
    <% if (typeof canTakeExam !== 'undefined' && canTakeExam) { %>
      <button class="btn btn-next" onclick="showTest()">Go to Final Exam → 📝</button>
    <% } else if (!user) { %>
      <a href="/signup" class="btn" style="background:#16a34a">✨ Signup Free to Unlock Final Exam →</a>
    <% } else { %>
      <button class="btn btn-locked" onclick="alert('Locked! Complete Lesson 1-49 with 80%+ first. You have passed <%= typeof passedCount !== 'undefined' ? passedCount : 0 %>/49.')">🔒 Final Exam Locked - <%= typeof passedCount !== 'undefined' ? passedCount : 0 %>/49 Passed</button>
    <% } %>
    <div class="nav">
      <a class="btn btn-prev" href="/lesson49">← Lesson 49</a>
      <a class="btn btn-next" href="/">🏠 Back to Home</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div id="testContent">
    <% if (typeof canTakeExam !== 'undefined' && canTakeExam) { %>
    <div class="test-box">
      <div style="background:#dcfce7;color:#166534;padding:12px;border-radius:10px;margin-bottom:14px;text-align:center;font-weight:bold;font-size:14px">✅ Logged in as <b><%= user.username %></b> - Your score will be saved & Certificate will be generated</div>
      <h2>📝 Final Exam - Lesson 50 - Become a Web Developer</h2>
      <div class="test-info"><b>Total Questions:</b> 20 &nbsp; | &nbsp; <b>Total Marks:</b> 100 &nbsp; | &nbsp; <b>Passing Marks:</b> 80 (80%) &nbsp; | &nbsp; <b>Time:</b> 10 Minutes<br>Each correct answer = 5 Marks. You need 16 correct to pass and get certificate. Once you start, all tabs will be locked until you submit.</div>
      <div id="startScreen">
        <h2>Ready for Final Exam? 🎓</h2>
        <p>You have completed 50 lessons. This is your final test.<br>Click Start Exam to begin. You will get <b>10 Minutes</b> for 20 questions.<br>Pass with 80% and get your certificate!</p>
        <button class="btn" style="font-size:20px;padding:14px 30px" onclick="startTest()">▶ Start Final Exam</button>
      </div>
      <div id="timerBar">⏰ Time Left: <span id="timerText">10:00</span></div>
      <div id="quizArea">
        <form id="quizForm">
          <div class="question"><b>Q1. What does HTML do?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q1" value="a"> Structure of website - Headings, paragraphs, links, images</label><label><input type="radio" name="q1" value="b"> Design / colors</label><label><input type="radio" name="q1" value="c"> Logic / interaction</label><label><input type="radio" name="q1" value="d"> Database</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q2. What does CSS do?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q2" value="a"> Design - Colors, layout, fonts, spacing</label><label><input type="radio" name="q2" value="b"> Structure</label><label><input type="radio" name="q2" value="c"> Logic</label><label><input type="radio" name="q2" value="d"> Server</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q3. What does JavaScript do?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q3" value="a"> Logic + Interaction - Clicks, cart, filter, validation</label><label><input type="radio" name="q3" value="b"> Structure only</label><label><input type="radio" name="q3" value="c"> Colors only</label><label><input type="radio" name="q3" value="d"> Nothing</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q4. How many H1 per page for SEO?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q4" value="a"> One H1 only</label><label><input type="radio" name="q4" value="b"> 5 H1s</label><label><input type="radio" name="q4" value="c"> 0 H1s</label><label><input type="radio" name="q4" value="d"> 10 H1s</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q5. Box Model?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q5" value="a"> Content + Padding + Border + Margin</label><label><input type="radio" name="q5" value="b"> Only content</label><label><input type="radio" name="q5" value="c"> Only margin</label><label><input type="radio" name="q5" value="d"> Only padding</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q6. Flexbox vs Grid?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q6" value="a"> Flexbox = 1D, Grid = 2D</label><label><input type="radio" name="q6" value="b"> Both same</label><label><input type="radio" name="q6" value="c"> Flexbox = 2D, Grid = 1D</label><label><input type="radio" name="q6" value="d"> No difference</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q7. How to make website responsive?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q7" value="a"> @media (max-width: 700px) - Change layout on small screens</label><label><input type="radio" name="q7" value="b"> Fixed width 2000px</label><label><input type="radio" name="q7" value="c"> No CSS</label><label><input type="radio" name="q7" value="d"> Only desktop</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q8. let vs const?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q8" value="a"> let = Can change, const = Cannot change</label><label><input type="radio" name="q8" value="b"> Both same</label><label><input type="radio" name="q8" value="c"> let = Cannot change</label><label><input type="radio" name="q8" value="d"> const = Can change</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q9. == vs === ?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q9" value="a"> == value only, === value + type - Always use ===</label><label><input type="radio" name="q9" value="b"> Both same</label><label><input type="radio" name="q9" value="c"> == is better</label><label><input type="radio" name="q9" value="d"> No difference</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q10. How to get element by id in JS?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q10" value="a"> document.getElementById("myId")</label><label><input type="radio" name="q10" value="b"> document.getId()</label><label><input type="radio" name="q10" value="c"> getElement("myId")</label><label><input type="radio" name="q10" value="d"> document.id("myId")</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q11. What is localStorage?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q11" value="a"> Browser storage - Saves data after refresh, 5MB</label><label><input type="radio" name="q11" value="b"> Deletes on refresh</label><label><input type="radio" name="q11" value="c"> Server storage</label><label><input type="radio" name="q11" value="d"> Only 1 second</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q12. What is a Portfolio?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q12" value="a"> Online shop window - Shows best work to get clients/jobs</label><label><input type="radio" name="q12" value="b"> Paper CV only</label><label><input type="radio" name="q12" value="c"> Social post</label><label><input type="radio" name="q12" value="d"> Certificate only</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q13. What is a Landing Page?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q13" value="a"> One page, one goal, one button - Buy / Sign Up / Order</label><label><input type="radio" name="q13" value="b"> Many pages, many goals</label><label><input type="radio" name="q13" value="c"> Only footer</label><label><input type="radio" name="q13" value="d"> Only contact</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q14. How to make sticky navbar?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q14" value="a"> position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 100;</label><label><input type="radio" name="q14" value="b"> position: static;</label><label><input type="radio" name="q14" value="c"> position: relative;</label><label><input type="radio" name="q14" value="d"> display: none;</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q15. What is SEO?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q15" value="a"> Make Google show YOUR website first</label><label><input type="radio" name="q15" value="b"> Make website colorful</label><label><input type="radio" name="q15" value="c"> Make website slow</label><label><input type="radio" name="q15" value="d"> Make website with no content</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q16. What must main file be named to deploy?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q16" value="a"> index.html</label><label><input type="radio" name="q16" value="b"> mywebsite.html</label><label><input type="radio" name="q16" value="c"> home.html</label><label><input type="radio" name="q16" value="d"> main.html</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q17. Freelancing payment rule?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q17" value="a"> 50% advance BEFORE starting, 50% after delivery</label><label><input type="radio" name="q17" value="b"> 100% after delivery</label><label><input type="radio" name="q17" value="c"> Work free</label><label><input type="radio" name="q17" value="d"> No payment</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q18. How to reverse string "Ali" in JS?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q18" value="a"> "Ali".split("").reverse().join("") = "ilA"</label><label><input type="radio" name="q18" value="b"> "Ali".reverse()</label><label><input type="radio" name="q18" value="c"> reverse("Ali")</label><label><input type="radio" name="q18" value="d"> "Ali".split()</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q19. How to add item to cart array?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q19" value="a"> cart.push(product)</label><label><input type="radio" name="q19" value="b"> cart.add(product)</label><label><input type="radio" name="q19" value="c"> cart.put(product)</label><label><input type="radio" name="q19" value="d"> cart += product</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q20. Best title length for SEO?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q20" value="a"> 50-60 characters, keyword first</label><label><input type="radio" name="q20" value="b"> 5 characters</label><label><input type="radio" name="q20" value="c"> 200 characters</label><label><input type="radio" name="q20" value="d"> No title</label></div>
          <button type="button" class="btn" onclick="checkTest(false)">Submit Final Exam - Get Certificate</button>
          <button type="button" class="btn btn-next" onclick="resetTest()">Try Again</button>
        </form>
      </div>
      <div id="scoreBox">
        <h3 id="scoreText"></h3>
        <p id="scoreMsg"></p>
        <div id="certSuccess" style="display:none">
          <p style="font-size:18px">🎓 <b>Your Certificate is Ready!</b> Your Certificate ID is <b id="newCertIdText"></b>. Enter your name in Lesson tab, then Print / Save as PDF.</p>
          <button class="btn" onclick="showLesson();document.getElementById('certPreview').scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth'})">View My Certificate 🎓</button>
          <button class="btn btn-next" onclick="window.print()">🖨️ Print / Save Certificate</button>
          <a id="newVerifyLink" href="#" target="_blank" class="btn" style="background:#f59e0b;color:#0f172a">🔍 Verify Certificate →</a>
        </div>
        <br><br>
        <button class="btn btn-next" onclick="showLesson()">← Back to Lesson (Unlocked)</button>
      </div>
    </div>
    <% } else { %>
      <div class="test-box" style="text-align:center">
        <h2>🔒 Final Exam Locked!</h2>
        <% if (!user) { %>
          <p>Final Exam is only for students who have <b>logged in</b> and passed <b>Lesson 1 to 49 with 80% or more.</b></p>
          <p>Please login or signup free to start your journey.</p>
          <a href="/signup" class="btn" style="background:#16a34a">✨ Signup Free →</a>
          <a href="/login" class="btn btn-next">Login →</a>
          <a href="/lesson1" class="btn">Start Lesson 1 →</a>
        <% } else { %>
          <p>Final Exam is only for students who have passed <b>Lesson 1 to 49 with 80% or more.</b></p>
          <p>Your Progress: <b><%= typeof passedCount !== 'undefined' ? passedCount : 0 %> / 49 Passed</b></p>
          <% if (typeof failedLessons !== 'undefined' && failedLessons.length > 0) { %>
            <p>Remaining Lessons: <b><%= failedLessons.join(', ') %></b></p>
          <% } %>
          <a href="/dashboard" class="btn btn-next">Check Dashboard →</a>
          <a href="/lesson<%= (typeof failedLessons !== 'undefined' && failedLessons.length > 0) ? failedLessons[0] : 1 %>" class="btn">Continue Learning →</a>
        <% } %>
      </div>
    <% } %>
  </div>
</div>

